WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.921 --> 00:00:19.851
The next morning Mary woke up when a young housemaid came into her room.

2
00:00:20.932 --> 00:00:25.935
While the young maid cleaned up the cinders in the fireplace, Mary lay in bed and looked around

3
00:00:26.015 --> 00:00:26.756
the gloomy room.

4
00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:32.140
The walls were covered with strange tapestries embroidered with forest scenes.

5
00:00:33.676 --> 00:00:36.258
Through a window she could see a great stretch of land.

6
00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:40.080
It looked like an endless, dull purple sea.

7
00:00:41.161 --> 00:00:41.942
"What is that?"

8
00:00:42.482 --> 00:00:43.783
Mary pointed out the window.

9
00:00:43.803 --> 00:00:48.886
"That's the moor," said the housemaid with a grin.

10
00:00:48.906 --> 00:00:50.107
"Do you like it?"

11
00:00:50.628 --> 00:00:51.969
"No. I hate it."

12
00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:55.871
"That's because you're not used to it.

13
00:00:56.932 --> 00:00:58.993
You think it's too big and bare now.

14
00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:00.654
But you will like it."

15
00:01:00.674 --> 00:01:02.636
"Do you like it?"

16
00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.773
"I do," said the housemaid.

17
00:01:05.793 --> 00:01:10.796
"In the spring it's covered with growing things that smell sweet.

18
00:01:11.776 --> 00:01:15.198
There's lots of fresh air, and the sky looks so high.

19
00:01:16.319 --> 00:01:18.780
I wouldn't live away from the moor for anything."

20
00:01:20.181 --> 00:01:24.003
As the maid lit the fire, Mary listened to her with a puzzled expression.

21
00:01:25.164 --> 00:01:27.005
Servants in India were not like this.

22
00:01:28.185 --> 00:01:32.628
Her nanny and the others did not talk to their masters in such a friendly way.

23
00:01:33.764 --> 00:01:34.524
"What's your name?"

24
00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:35.705
Mary asked.

25
00:01:35.725 --> 00:01:37.665
"Are you going to be my servant?"

26
00:01:37.685 --> 00:01:39.866
"I'm Martha.

27
00:01:40.406 --> 00:01:43.407
I'll do the housemaid's work up here and wait on you a bit.

28
00:01:44.427 --> 00:01:46.288
But you won't need much waiting on."

29
00:01:47.268 --> 00:01:48.728
"Who is going to dress me?"

30
00:01:49.148 --> 00:01:50.109
demanded Mary.

31
00:01:51.169 --> 00:01:52.969
Martha looked at Mary in amazement.

32
00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:56.510
"Can't you dress yourself?"

33
00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.891
"No. My nanny dressed me, of course."

34
00:01:58.911 --> 00:02:03.961
"Well," said Martha bluntly, "it's time you learned."

35
00:02:05.443 --> 00:02:07.504
Martha helped Mary get dressed that morning.

36
00:02:08.645 --> 00:02:12.528
Then they went into the next room, where she set out Mary's breakfast on a table.

37
00:02:12.548 --> 00:02:15.751
"I don't want it," said Mary.

38
00:02:15.771 --> 00:02:18.193
"You don't want your porridge!"

39
00:02:18.753 --> 00:02:20.054
Martha couldn't believe this.

40
00:02:20.074 --> 00:02:22.737
"You don't know how good it is.

41
00:02:23.257 --> 00:02:24.578
Put a bit of sugar on it."

42
00:02:25.899 --> 00:02:27.120
But Mary refused.

43
00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:34.877
"If my brothers and sisters were here," said Martha, "they'd clean this table bare in five minutes."

44
00:02:36.118 --> 00:02:39.639
"Why?" "Because they never have enough to eat.

45
00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.880
I am one of 12 children.

46
00:02:42.841 --> 00:02:45.402
My father gets only a small wage each week.

47
00:02:46.742 --> 00:02:51.904
The children play on the moor all day, and my mother says the air of the moor fattens

48
00:02:51.944 --> 00:02:52.305
them up.

49
00:02:53.325 --> 00:02:56.987
She thinks they must eat the grass the same as the wild ponies do.

50
00:02:58.087 --> 00:03:02.902
My brother Dickon is 12 years old, and he has a young pony he calls his own."

51
00:03:02.922 --> 00:03:05.223
"Where did he get the pony?"

52
00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:06.404
asked Mary.

53
00:03:07.425 --> 00:03:10.527
She was amazed at how this servant talked on and on.

54
00:03:10.547 --> 00:03:14.390
"Dickon found it on the moor with its mother.

55
00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:20.354
He gave it bread and new grass, so now it follows him around and lets him sit on

56
00:03:20.414 --> 00:03:21.014
its back.

57
00:03:22.075 --> 00:03:24.777
Dickon's a kind lad, and animals like him."

58
00:03:25.817 --> 00:03:29.460
Mary had never had a pet of her own, but she'd always wanted one.

59
00:03:30.632 --> 00:03:32.753
She began to be a little interested in Dickon.

60
00:03:34.154 --> 00:03:35.175
This was something new.

61
00:03:36.135 --> 00:03:39.497
The only person she'd ever been interested in before was herself.

62
00:03:40.698 --> 00:03:43.539
She drank some tea and ate some toast with marmalade.

63
00:03:43.559 --> 00:03:48.162
"You wrap up warmly and run out to play now," said Martha.

64
00:03:48.182 --> 00:03:51.584
"It'll do you good and give you an appetite."

65
00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:55.526
Mary went to the window and looked out.

66
00:03:56.606 --> 00:04:01.725
She saw gardens and paths and big trees, but everything looked dull and wintry.

67
00:04:01.745 --> 00:04:04.767
"Why should I go out on a day like this?"

68
00:04:04.787 --> 00:04:10.590
"Well, if you don't go out, you'll have to stay in, and what is there to do here?"

69
00:04:12.071 --> 00:04:13.052
Mary looked around.

70
00:04:13.532 --> 00:04:14.772
There was nothing to do.

71
00:04:14.792 --> 00:04:16.754
"But who will go out with me?"

72
00:04:16.774 --> 00:04:19.915
"You'll have to learn to play by yourself.

73
00:04:20.996 --> 00:04:24.958
Our Dickon goes off on the moor and plays by himself for hours.

74
00:04:26.179 --> 00:04:28.160
That's how he made friends with the pony.

75
00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:34.029
He has sheep on the moor that know him and birds that come and eat from his hand."

76
00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:40.771
It was this mention of Dickon that made Mary decide to go out, though she was not aware

77
00:04:40.811 --> 00:04:41.051
of it.

78
00:04:42.092 --> 00:04:43.712
Perhaps she would see some birds.

79
00:04:44.873 --> 00:04:49.034
They would be different from those in India, and it might amuse her to look at them.

80
00:04:50.614 --> 00:04:52.695
Martha found Mary's coat and hat for her.

81
00:04:53.795 --> 00:04:56.736
Then Martha showed Mary the way downstairs and outside.

82
00:04:57.812 --> 00:05:03.274
"If you go around that way, you'll come to the gardens," she said, pointing to a gate in

83
00:05:03.314 --> 00:05:04.434
a wall of shrubbery.

84
00:05:04.454 --> 00:05:07.295
"One of the gardens is locked up.

85
00:05:07.775 --> 00:05:10.355
No one has been in it for ten years."

86
00:05:12.296 --> 00:05:13.976
"Why?" "Mr.

87
00:05:14.056 --> 00:05:16.737
Craven shut it when his wife died suddenly.

88
00:05:17.277 --> 00:05:18.398
It was her garden.

89
00:05:19.498 --> 00:05:23.439
He locked the door and then buried the key so no one could go inside.

90
00:05:25.339 --> 00:05:25.840
There's Mrs.

91
00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.940
Medlock's bell ringing.

92
00:05:27.317 --> 00:05:28.039
I must run."

93
00:05:29.082 --> 00:05:34.079
And with that Martha was off, leaving Mary to wander outside by herself.
